From: edde746 <86283021+edde746@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] vd_lavc: do not decode the first H.264 packet twice with a hardware decoder

demux_mkv hands the decoder the first packet of an H.264 track
(probe_x264_garbage, sh->codec->first_packet), and init_avctx() decodes
and flushes it right after avcodec_open2(): the x264 build number in its
SEI turns on libavcodec's workaround for the 4:4:4 streams of old x264
builds. That workaround is libavcodec's own reconstruction, which a
hardware decoder never runs, but the decode ran all the same: get_format,
a VideoToolbox session (or a MediaCodec), one frame decoded and thrown
away, and then all of it again for the first real packet. An iPhone's log
of an H.264 Matroska file has "Requesting pixfmt 'videotoolbox_vld'" and
"Reinit context" twice, 15 and 10 ms apart, and FILE_LOADED comes 12 ms later
than for the same streams in MP4, which has no first_packet.

Skip that decode while a hardware decoder is being tried. One that fails
falls back through init_avctx() with use_hwdec unset, so software
decoding gets the packet as before.

iPhone Air, H.264 1080p in Matroska, ms after loadfile, medians of 3
interleaved runs, Plezy's / Tortuga's option set, before -> after:
FILE_LOADED 23.7 -> 7.5 / 24.4 -> 6.8 with the audio session active and
34.8 -> 11.9 / 34.6 -> 11.6 when the audio output activates it;
PLAYBACK_RESTART 55.1 -> 48.4 / 51.3 -> 44.6 and 103.5 -> 97.1 /
100.4 -> 89.7; a second player in the process 88.8 -> 79.2 / 85.1 -> 73.4.
The same streams in MP4 do not change (48.9 -> 46.1 / 47.1 -> 46.8 with
the rest of this series' startup patches).

diff --git a/video/decode/vd_lavc.c b/video/decode/vd_lavc.c
index 202f726..c89ae22 100644
--- a/video/decode/vd_lavc.c
+++ b/video/decode/vd_lavc.c
@@ -870,7 +870,12 @@ static void init_avctx(struct mp_filter *vd)
     // decoding of the rest of the stream. The only currently known case is the
     // x264 build number (encoded in a SEI element), needed to enable a
     // workaround for broken 4:4:4 streams produced by older x264 versions.
-    if (lavc_codec->id == AV_CODEC_ID_H264 && c->first_packet) {
+    // That workaround is libavcodec's own reconstruction, which a hardware
+    // decoder does not use; with one, decoding the packet here would open the
+    // hardware decoder, decode the frame and flush it, only for the first real
+    // packet to open it again. A hardware decoder that fails falls back
+    // through this function with use_hwdec unset, and takes the packet then.
+    if (lavc_codec->id == AV_CODEC_ID_H264 && c->first_packet && !ctx->use_hwdec) {
         mp_set_av_packet(ctx->avpkt, c->first_packet, &ctx->codec_timebase);
         avcodec_send_packet(avctx, ctx->avpkt);
         avcodec_receive_frame(avctx, ctx->pic);
